          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Approximately 3–4 weeks of anteromedial left heel pain, described as like standing on a stone. Especially painful with first steps in the morning and after prolonged sitting in the patrol car. Eases after 10–15 minutes of walking, with a dull ache by the end of the shift. Worse with long shifts, foot patrol, and heavy boots.",
